+### Compound Durations
+
+Use `parseCompound` to sum several pieces into one value. Pieces can be separated by whitespace, commas, or nothing at all. When there is more than one piece, each needs a unit.
+
+```ts
+import { parseCompound } from 'ms';
+
+parseCompound('1h 30m'); // 5400000
+parseCompound('1h, 30m'); // 5400000
+parseCompound('2 days 4 hours'); // 187200000
+parseCompound('1h30m15s'); // 5415000
+```
+
+It throws a `TypeError` if the string can't be parsed.
+
 ### Enhanced Type Safety
 
 If you want strict type checking for the input value, you can use `parseStrict`.
